This appears to be from a CBP ruling or a Commerce scope ruling on Belleville washers. Classification options: 7318.21 (spring washers and other lock washers) versus 7320 (springs). Because the description says it is a type of lock washer, 7318.21 applies. The subheading 7318.21.00 is split into statistical suffixes: 7318.21.0030 for "Of iron or steel, spring washers and other lock washers: Belleville washers" (I recall 7318.21.0030 as Belleville), while 7318.21.0090 is "other". Stainless steel is still iron or steel, so that suffix applies.

The 2022 HTS has 7318.21.00 with these suffixes: 7318.21.0030 "Belleville washers" and 7318.21.0090 "Other". Both of those sit under 7318.21.00 in the "Threaded articles" and "Non-threaded articles" structure. I'm going with 7318.21.0030.

{"hts_code": "7318.21.0030", "reason": "A stainless-steel Belleville washer is a spring/lock washer, which falls under heading 7318 (non-threaded articles), subheading 7318.21 (spring washers and other lock washers), with the specific statistical suffix for Belleville washers."}
